{
  "case_id": "2009-08-680",
  "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is our position that a break in custody from custodial interrogation should be the bright line that this Court adopts in order to end the irrebuttable presumption that this Court created in the Edwards case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, we do think one day should be enough, as long as it is not in the pretrial detention category."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is the rationale for the break in custody that there is a likelihood of non-coercion? Is that the reason that you offer for the rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But if the defendant goes home, he can contact a lawyer. In prison he can't do that. So, if the whole idea is to protect his right to counsel, then it makes a big difference whether he's at home or in prison."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF TOBY J. HEYTENS ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the reason that this case matters in an intensely practical way is, there are approximately a million and a half prison inmates in this country right now, many of whom are serving extremely long sentences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But the record doesn't tell us whether he was given an opportunity to say \"I don't want any visitors today.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. DAVIS",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. DAVIS: No, it does not, but I think the State has the burden to show. The circumstances --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Or -- or do you ask him, are you willing to speak to investigators about a crime? And he says what crime? I mean, how specific does -- does the request for permission to have visitors have to be?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. DAVIS",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. DAVIS: Well, it does present some tensions with Roberson. However, in this case, since it is limited to the same crime, does it extend as far as Roberson does? And I would like to answer Justice Stevens' question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What would be a serious -- what would be a serious answer to that question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your adversary says that they -- he can't change his mind. It has to be a spontaneous, you know, somehow they have to be in a room together that wasn't planned and he has to come up and say, I am confessing out of the kindness of my heart."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Davis",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is the badgering. That is the specter of coercion that is inconsistent with the Constitutional right related to Miranda to have counsel present."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My thought is, can you use the rule for lawyers, which has worked, to help shape a rule that would work here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a4ac25fd94d7a7cfd41a53516e7bffeb9f7863e89933fa654beb3c2e1305fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a4ac25fd94d-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thank you, Counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-680",
      "confidence": 0.0,
